From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Playport <dev@playport.invalid>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 18:33:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: protect owned WoW64 window pages per Wine page

Native NtProtectVirtualMemory on an owner's i386 window handled only
anonymous VM, in whole 16 KiB host pages, and refused WRITECOPY and
PAGE_GUARD. Wine's image setup set window image protections through the
generic set_vprot, whose byte union lets a guard page revoke its host
page and whose failures were ignored. The WoW64 loader will protect
image and heap pages at 4 KiB, so give both kinds of window storage the
same transaction:

- Wine (4 KiB) pages keep their logical protection, including EXEC,
  WRITECOPY and GUARD, and queries report it per page. A 16 KiB host
  page gets the union of its pages' native permissions, never EXEC:
  execute-only pages stay readable for FEX's decoder. A host page whose
  committed guard page would sit beside an accessible page is refused,
  so a guard page is always enforced.
- Image pages take READWRITE as WRITECOPY, as Wine does; anonymous VM
  refuses WRITECOPY. Backing is never replaced: a private image page
  becomes writable MAP_PRIVATE or anonymous memory, so writes stay a
  private copy. Images with shared writable sections are refused at
  map time.
- Every host page is checked before any changes, each changes with its
  own mprotect, a failure restores the pages already changed, and page
  bytes and caller outputs change only on success. The old protection
  is the first page's. Free space, the low guard and ranges leaving one
  allocation are invalid; bootstrap TEB/PEB views, quarantined images,
  padding past the server's image extent and cache/CFG modifiers are
  not supported.
- Wine's image setup and anonymous commit use the same transaction, and
  a failed protection now fails a window image map. mprotect_range
  (fault and helper paths) uses the same per-page policy.

Wine's protection conversions move unchanged into wow64_vprot.h so that
host tests compile them.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-03-portal2-wine-window.md
Offered-upstream: no (Playport's owner-local iOS WoW64 window)
